{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":56524,"duration_api_ms":56178,"num_turns":6,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"52fda848-8505-46d0-a427-1cc4f3bf7069","total_cost_usd":0.29988325,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":28597,"cache_read_input_tokens":117604,"output_tokens":2493,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":28597,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":5,"outputTokens":2493,"cacheReadInputTokens":117604,"cacheCreationInputTokens":28597,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.29988325,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"All three amendments correctly identify test-validity regressions where assertions and/or setup no longer match the documented behavior under test. Each was verified against the source: (1) the biofilter probe's assertion allows the large-filter run to have less nitrifier biomass than the small, contradicting its documented purpose; (2) the redox probe seeds denitrifier_activity_index at 1.0 making the maturation ramp unreachable; (3) the planted-substrate probe has a 5× decomposer biomass confound and zero plant biomass, so the comparison tests decomposer-driven suboxia rather than planted-substrate properties.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-4-08002dd1","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified. Lines 153-166 document that 2× media should yield 'comparable or more nitrifier biomass,' but lines 244-263 only assert both exceed a 0.02g floor. The inline comment at 244-247 acknowledges that the large filter may have lower density due to nutrient limitation, but the assertion doesn't enforce 'comparable' in any meaningful way — it allows arbitrarily less biomass in the large run. A regression that broke media-area scaling of nitrifier carrying capacity would pass undetected. The assertion or documentation needs realignment."},{"amendment_id":"fr-4-e772c7bf","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified. Line 661 seeds denitrifier_activity_index = 1.0, and the update_daily_denitrifier_activity function (nitrogen_cycle.rs:973-989) computes daily_rate * (target - prev) where target = 1.0 when a suboxic zone exists. With prev = 1.0 and target = 1.0, the delta is zero — the maturation ramp is never exercised. The assertion at lines 851-853 (> 0.5) would pass even if the daily update function were entirely removed, since starting at 1.0 trivially satisfies > 0.5. Despite the docstring at line 633 claiming it validates that 'denitrifier activity index matures over time,' the test does not exercise maturation at all."},{"amendment_id":"fr-4-d4d1e581","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified. The planted arm (line 664) gets decomposer_biomass_g = 10.0 while the inert arm (line 743) gets 2.0 — a 5× difference. substrate.rs:221-236 confirms decomposer biomass directly drives substrate O₂ demand, which determines O₂ penetration depth and therefore suboxic zone volume. This 5× decomposer imbalance alone produces a much larger suboxic zone in the planted arm, enabling denitrification regardless of whether the ActivePlanted substrate type contributes anything. Furthermore, lines 711-713 zero all plant biomass, so the 'planted' arm has no live plants — the substrate type label ActivePlanted is the only planted element, making the test name misleading. A regression in ActivePlanted-specific logic would be masked by the decomposer confound."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"5a4714a4-bbec-4a14-bcbf-4780ed240dfb"}
